{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"diagnosis\":\"The structural induction is valid, but `grind` cannot reduce the `substOld` application match when the function and argument are known only through branch equalities. Explicitly splitting that match and its identifier test lets `simp_all` expose the replacement-variable membership case; the remaining constructor cases are discharged as before.\",\"proof_body\":\"by\\n  intro v Hin\\n  induction post <;>\\n    simp [OldExpressions.substOld,\\n      Imperative.HasVarsPure.getVars,\\n      Lambda.LExpr.LExpr.getVars] at *\\n  case app fn e fn_ih e_ih =>\\n    split at Hin\\n    · split at Hin <;>\\n        simp_all [Imperative.HasVarsPure.getVars,\\n          Lambda.LExpr.LExpr.getVars]\\n    · simp [Imperative.HasVarsPure.getVars,\\n          Lambda.LExpr.LExpr.getVars] at Hin ⊢\\n      rcases Hin with Hin | Hin\\n      · rcases fn_ih Hin with Hin | Hin\\n        · exact Or.inl (Or.inl Hin)\\n        · exact Or.inr Hin\\n      · rcases e_ih Hin with Hin | Hin\\n        · exact Or.inl (Or.inr Hin)\\n        · exact Or.inr Hin\\n  all_goals grind\"}"}}
